    "body": "The Zarr and NetCDF writers fall back to `string(x)` for grid constructor arguments they do not recognize.\r\n\r\nThis PR writes any `AbstractVerticalCoordinate` as its type name plus reference interfaces, e.g. `MutableVerticalDiscretization([-100.0, -50.0, 0.0])`, and whitelists `MutableVerticalDiscretization` in the serialized-output reader so mutable grids round-trip through `reconstruct_grid`, which previously failed to parse their printed form.",
